Z||000002||Gold-86SE||06-29-2000||12:06 PM||||<BR>I guess it depends on what type of information you are looking for, but here is some minor information.<P>There were two engines available in 86:<BR>2.5L in-line 4 with 92HP, and<BR>2.8L V6 with 140HP.<P>Tranny options were these:<BR>3 speed auto, available on all models.<BR>For the 4-cylinder, a 5 speed manual was available all year long <BR>For the V6, a 4 speed manual was available until about mid-year, and then a 5 speed manual was introduced around 86.5.<P>There were several body styles available:<BR>the entry coupe, which has the black bumper nose and tail<BR>the SE, which is the same as the '85 GT<BR>the GT, which is the same as the SE, except the GT is now a Fastback style.<P>Wheel options that I know of, were:<BR>13" wheels may have come on the entry level coupes<BR>14" Hi-tech Turbo, and<BR>15" Lace, found on the GT<P>Additionally, check out my website <A HREF="http://www.thefieroclub.com/members/~fieromag/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thefieroclub.com/members/~fieromag/index.html</A>  click on "Articles" then go to the  "Information From Pontiac" and you will find specifications for the 86 year model.<P>For further information, ask a specific, or semi-specific question and we can get the answer for you.<P>BTW, welcome to the forum and glad to have another member in the Fiero family.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 06-29-2000).]||||reg||1
